  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>When glucose is treated with dilute&nbsp;NaOH, it&nbsp;gives a&nbsp;mixture of&nbsp;D-glucose,&nbsp;D-mannose and&nbsp;D-fructose. This reaction is known as Lobry de Bruyn-van Ekenstein rearrangement.&nbsp;Basic catalysed&nbsp;tautomerism through enediol intermediate takes place.<img src=\"assets\\st0003_e5944b0640d7.png\" style=\"width: 508px; height: 450px;\" /></p></blockquote>"
